1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,016
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:02,016
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,016 --> 00:00:03,049
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,049 --> 00:00:04,616
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

5
00:00:04,616 --> 00:00:06,916
[Episode 11]

6
00:00:16,028 --> 00:00:17,728
Let's go together!

7
00:00:21,048 --> 00:00:25,144
I told you to stay put and learn from
your new mentor. Why look for trouble?

8
00:00:25,144 --> 00:00:27,120
Where the needle goes,
the thread must follow.

9
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,416
What are you going to do without me?

10
00:00:31,756 --> 00:00:32,865
Being prepared?

11
00:00:32,865 --> 00:00:35,316
I've been ready for this for a million years!

12
00:00:35,316 --> 00:00:37,016
Keep your voice down.

13
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:42,473
Let's go catch Kingfisher.

14
00:00:42,473 --> 00:00:43,849
Yes, sir!

15
00:00:43,849 --> 00:00:45,549
[Police]

16
00:00:47,678 --> 00:00:49,716
Mr. Lee.

17
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:50,932
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

18
00:00:50,932 --> 00:00:54,049
<i>A special task force aimed at capturing
the armed serial killer "Kingfisher"</i>

19
00:00:54,049 --> 00:00:55,749
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
<i>was launched today</i>

20
00:00:55,749 --> 00:00:58,828
<i>at the Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency.</i>

21
00:00:58,828 --> 00:01:00,567
<i>This special task force will be</i>

22
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:01,860
[Gu Tae Seok]
<i>different from those of the past.</i>

23
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,444
[Head of the Kingfisher Task Force]
<i>We'll never create a task force</i>

24
00:01:03,444 --> 00:01:06,140
<i>just for show and quietly disband it later.</i>

25
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:08,104
<i>This time, we are committed to
seeing this through to the end,</i>

26
00:01:08,104 --> 00:01:10,216
<i>and we will devote
every available resource to it.</i>

27
00:01:10,216 --> 00:01:13,449
Is this the third time they've
promised to devote every resource?

28
00:01:13,449 --> 00:01:15,524
No, it's the fourth.

29
00:01:15,524 --> 00:01:17,913
They've been creating
and disbanding these task forces

30
00:01:17,913 --> 00:01:19,240
every three or four years or so.

31
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:21,748
What does "the end" mean this time?

32
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:23,616
<i>That's all.</i>

33
00:01:23,616 --> 00:01:25,883
[Past Cases Under Review
with New Investigative Techniques]

34
00:01:31,732 --> 00:01:37,149
This is Inspector Yoo Mi Ran, a profiler
with the Seoul Metropolitan Police.

35
00:01:37,149 --> 00:01:39,072
[Yoo Mi Ran]

36
00:01:39,072 --> 00:01:40,444
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
Well, you all know her, right?

37
00:01:40,444 --> 00:01:47,016
The celebrity cop who solved the 20-year-old
Oh Seong Gu serial murder case.

38
00:01:49,052 --> 00:01:53,692
I applied because I heard there was
no overtime and guaranteed time off.

39
00:01:53,692 --> 00:01:54,774
That's true, right?

40
00:01:54,774 --> 00:01:57,016
- Really?
- It's not?

41
00:01:57,016 --> 00:02:00,636
Oh, that's not good.
I might have to quit already.

42
00:02:00,636 --> 00:02:03,292
All right, now that
we've introduced ourselves,

43
00:02:03,292 --> 00:02:04,292
let's get down to business.

44
00:02:04,292 --> 00:02:06,349
[Discussion of Kingfisher Suspect Pool]

45
00:02:10,648 --> 00:02:14,149
No matter how I look at it,
I just don't understand.

46
00:02:15,436 --> 00:02:20,620
Didn't he, in a way, avenge the person
who killed his own parents?

47
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:24,880
How can he arrest someone like that
with his own hands?

48
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,048
Even if he's a police officer.

49
00:02:27,048 --> 00:02:29,824
Is avenging someone's grudge what you do?

50
00:02:29,824 --> 00:02:32,783
No, it's not like that.

51
00:02:32,783 --> 00:02:36,900
Everyone just chooses their own path
for their own reasons.

52
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:40,976
Some people can't be like us.

53
00:02:40,976 --> 00:02:43,868
And we just have to do our job.

54
00:02:43,868 --> 00:02:45,568
Right?

55
00:02:46,184 --> 00:02:47,884
Here.

56
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,192
It's noon. Let's eat!

57
00:02:52,192 --> 00:02:53,892
Oh, yeah?

58
00:02:54,888 --> 00:02:58,616
So, what should we have for lunch today?

59
00:02:58,616 --> 00:03:00,892
Wow, it's already this late?

60
00:03:00,892 --> 00:03:03,100
Lunchtime!

61
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,168
It's hot out. How about naengmyeon for lunch?

62
00:03:05,168 --> 00:03:06,284
Naengmyeon sounds great. Let's go.

63
00:03:06,284 --> 00:03:07,608
- Naengmyeon good.
- Come on, Manager Go, let's go.

64
00:03:07,608 --> 00:03:08,657
Alright.

65
00:03:08,657 --> 00:03:10,849
I want naengmyeon in chilled broth.

66
00:03:13,956 --> 00:03:17,076
I wonder if Manager Tae Min
is going to grab something quick again.

67
00:03:17,076 --> 00:03:20,096
Oh, I don't know how
he can eat in places like that.

68
00:03:20,096 --> 00:03:23,056
Don't worry. He'll be eating properly
for the time being.

69
00:03:23,056 --> 00:03:25,248
Huh? For the time being?

70
00:03:25,248 --> 00:03:26,948
Why?

71
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:18,852
[Discussion of Kingfisher Suspect Pool]
Kingfisher is a methodical killer

72
00:04:18,852 --> 00:04:22,164
who operates with a clear motive
and objective.

73
00:04:22,164 --> 00:04:26,644
His weapon of choice is a sniper rifle,
hard for civilians to obtain.

74
00:04:26,644 --> 00:04:29,903
Given the circumstances, we should
probably start from the fact that

75
00:04:29,903 --> 00:04:31,592
he's physically very capable, right?

76
00:04:31,592 --> 00:04:34,883
Special forces background
seems like the closest fit, doesn't it?

77
00:04:34,883 --> 00:04:37,516
I've already looked into that sector.

78
00:04:37,516 --> 00:04:39,682
I screened 400 individuals
who served in military special forces

79
00:04:39,682 --> 00:04:42,356
before Kingfisher first appeared in 2010,

80
00:04:42,356 --> 00:04:44,823
focusing on those
with exceptional marksmanship,

81
00:04:44,823 --> 00:04:46,516
and investigated them one by one.

82
00:04:46,516 --> 00:04:48,585
I found nothing.

83
00:04:48,585 --> 00:04:52,049
You were practically
looking for a needle in a haystack.

84
00:04:53,228 --> 00:04:58,716
So all 400 special forces veterans
were adult Korean men?

85
00:04:59,816 --> 00:05:03,100
Well, yes, naturally...

86
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:08,004
So are you saying Kingfisher
could be a woman or even a minor?

87
00:05:08,004 --> 00:05:09,749
What is this, a movie?

88
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,920
We shouldn't be constrained by the assumption

89
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,572
that Kingfisher is an adult Korean male.

90
00:05:16,572 --> 00:05:18,852
We need to keep every possibility open.

91
00:05:18,852 --> 00:05:23,464
Gender, age, nationality, and so on.

92
00:05:23,464 --> 00:05:25,556
<i>Kingfisher is...</i>

93
00:05:25,556 --> 00:05:27,649
a tall...

94
00:05:28,624 --> 00:05:33,449
well-built young man.

95
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:38,212
And there's one more thing
we need to pay attention to.

96
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:40,428
It's the cooling-off periods.

97
00:05:40,428 --> 00:05:43,583
You mean the Haegong-dong Gosiwon case?

98
00:05:43,583 --> 00:05:45,960
Well, you're right.

99
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:49,016
There was a four-year gap
in his activity after that.

100
00:05:49,016 --> 00:05:53,080
A serial killer's hiatus is usually
explained in one of two ways.

101
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,840
One is external control, like restrictions
from arrest or incarceration.

102
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:59,316
The other is an internal load state.

103
00:05:59,316 --> 00:06:05,149
When the desire is temporarily satisfied,
the impulse subsides.

104
00:06:05,964 --> 00:06:10,124
But I believe Kingfisher is different.

105
00:06:10,124 --> 00:06:11,152
Why?

106
00:06:11,152 --> 00:06:14,916
Because Kingfisher isn't

107
00:06:15,632 --> 00:06:17,332
an ordinary psychopath.

108
00:06:18,276 --> 00:06:20,480
You're suggesting there
may have been some change

109
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,616
in his state of mind or
his surrounding circumstances?

110
00:06:23,616 --> 00:06:24,616
Exactly.

111
00:06:24,616 --> 00:06:27,272
[Analysis of Cooling-Off Periods]

112
00:06:27,272 --> 00:06:29,008
There was another one
besides Haegong-dong, right?

113
00:06:29,008 --> 00:06:30,137
[The two gaps may provide clues]
Eight years ago,

114
00:06:30,137 --> 00:06:32,188
[to Kingfisher's true identity]
the so-called "World Cup incident"

115
00:06:32,188 --> 00:06:34,680
was followed by a nine-month gap.

116
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:37,736
Given that his previous crime intervals
were no more than two months,

117
00:06:37,736 --> 00:06:41,196
it's clearly... a significant figure.

118
00:06:41,196 --> 00:06:45,752
So, I believe these two gaps,
one long and one short,

119
00:06:45,752 --> 00:06:51,083
may provide clues to
Kingfisher's true identity.

120
00:06:52,048 --> 00:06:55,980
Okay, just as Ms. Yoo suggested,
let's keep open the possibility that

121
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,764
Kingfisher could be a woman or even a minor,

122
00:06:57,764 --> 00:06:59,528
and look more closely at the commonalities

123
00:06:59,528 --> 00:07:01,708
between the World Cup and Haegong-dong cases.

124
00:07:01,708 --> 00:07:03,764
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, understood.

125
00:07:03,764 --> 00:07:05,483
- Yes.
- Understood.

126
00:07:07,612 --> 00:07:09,470
<i>The World Cup case and the Haegong-dong case.</i>

127
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,960
You were there for both major incidents.

128
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,454
The odds of that are practically impossible.

129
00:07:13,454 --> 00:07:16,049
I'm a reporter, you punk!

130
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,888
<i>I heard your reporter friend woke up.</i>

131
00:07:31,888 --> 00:07:32,932
That's a relief.

132
00:07:32,932 --> 00:07:35,324
Oh, he barely made it back
from the brink of death.

133
00:07:35,324 --> 00:07:39,216
Oh, did he find his savior? The person
who called an ambulance for him.

134
00:07:39,216 --> 00:07:40,500
Oh, that woman?

135
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,949
She made the call from my friend's phone,
so it's difficult to identify her.

136
00:07:47,788 --> 00:07:52,649
But apparently that's the building
where Kingfisher took the shot,

137
00:07:52,649 --> 00:07:54,432
and the timing roughly lines up too.

138
00:07:54,432 --> 00:08:00,049
I was wondering if Kingfisher
might have made the call.

139
00:08:00,828 --> 00:08:05,080
Killed someone from above
and saved a life on the way down?

140
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:07,040
And a woman, no less?

141
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,383
Yes.

142
00:08:08,383 --> 00:08:10,016
Oh, for God's sake.

143
00:08:10,016 --> 00:08:11,486
Stop chasing wild theories
about someone else's case

144
00:08:11,486 --> 00:08:13,649
and focus on your own case, punk.

145
00:08:25,983 --> 00:08:28,049
[City Mania Hotel Incident]

146
00:08:35,083 --> 00:08:37,849
[Witness Interview Report]

147
00:08:39,796 --> 00:08:41,528
<i>Looking back later,</i>

148
00:08:41,528 --> 00:08:44,188
[Under Investigation]
all the security cameras were broken.

149
00:08:44,188 --> 00:08:46,024
I didn't know while I was on duty.

150
00:08:46,024 --> 00:08:48,416
The monitors appeared to be working normally.

151
00:08:48,416 --> 00:08:50,776
Was there absolutely
no one else in the building?

152
00:08:50,776 --> 00:08:52,452
Like the cleaning crew?

153
00:08:52,452 --> 00:08:57,140
There were no employees
working late that day.

154
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:59,208
<i>And the cleaning crew left early.</i>

155
00:08:59,208 --> 00:09:01,916
<i>They left before the crowds
started coming in.</i>

156
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:04,496
<i>It wasn't an employee or a cleaner.</i>

157
00:09:04,496 --> 00:09:06,316
<i>Then who was it?</i>

158
00:09:06,316 --> 00:09:09,056
<i>Who reported Tae Seong?</i>

159
00:09:09,056 --> 00:09:12,049
Oh, Kwon Se Ah is always busy.

160
00:09:18,652 --> 00:09:19,860
What are you looking for?

161
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,083
It's not here...

162
00:09:21,083 --> 00:09:23,204
The records related to Tae Seong's case...

163
00:09:23,204 --> 00:09:25,260
Tae Seong?

164
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:26,802
Oh, you mean the case where he was mugged

165
00:09:26,802 --> 00:09:29,028
while chasing a pickpocket
during the World Cup?

166
00:09:29,028 --> 00:09:32,300
Why is that in there?
It wasn't even a Kingfisher case.

167
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:35,276
Could those two cases be unrelated?

168
00:09:35,276 --> 00:09:36,983
Or what?

169
00:09:45,516 --> 00:09:46,516
Where are you going?

170
00:09:46,516 --> 00:09:47,700
The prison.

171
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:48,824
Follow me if you want.

172
00:09:48,824 --> 00:09:50,184
What? Why a prison?

173
00:09:50,184 --> 00:09:51,260
Who is there?

174
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,283
Someone we excluded
from the investigation back then.

175
00:09:53,283 --> 00:09:55,824
So who is that? Huh?

176
00:10:09,464 --> 00:10:10,464
[Green Sky Welfare Center]

177
00:10:10,464 --> 00:10:11,616
<i>Her grandson?</i>

178
00:10:11,616 --> 00:10:13,783
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

179
00:10:13,783 --> 00:10:17,664
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

180
00:10:17,664 --> 00:10:19,728
Do you happen to know where he is now?

181
00:10:19,728 --> 00:10:21,849
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

182
00:10:21,849 --> 00:10:26,749
<i>Yeah. There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.</i>

183
00:10:30,908 --> 00:10:32,276
You said you came to see Cheol, right?

184
00:10:32,276 --> 00:10:34,336
Yes.

185
00:10:34,336 --> 00:10:37,016
That's him over there.

186
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:45,109
When he first came here,

187
00:10:45,109 --> 00:10:48,460
he struggled to express himself
and interact with others,

188
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,544
but he's much brighter now.

189
00:10:50,544 --> 00:10:52,176
That's good to hear.

190
00:10:52,176 --> 00:10:55,220
He seems to like drawing.

191
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,868
A sponsor sends him flowers every week,

192
00:10:57,868 --> 00:11:00,624
and on those days he always
draws flowers like that.

193
00:11:00,624 --> 00:11:01,964
A sponsor?

194
00:11:01,964 --> 00:11:07,649
There's an anonymous sponsor who funds
various treatment programs for Cheol.

195
00:11:08,936 --> 00:11:11,616
What is their relationship to the child?

196
00:11:11,616 --> 00:11:14,649
Well, I'm not sure about that.

197
00:11:17,252 --> 00:11:21,940
If you don't mind, could I meet them?

198
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:26,249
I'm afraid that's not possible.
They don't want anyone to know who they are.

199
00:11:33,016 --> 00:11:39,020
When sending flowers,
they always add a flower language card.

200
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:43,540
The very first time, there was
also a separate message card.

201
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:46,792
"I hope you find your own beautiful view."

202
00:11:46,792 --> 00:11:48,949
That was all it said.

203
00:11:53,549 --> 00:11:55,944
What did you just say?

204
00:11:55,944 --> 00:11:58,708
- Excuse me?
- The message on the first card they sent.

205
00:11:58,708 --> 00:12:02,749
"I hope you find your own
beautiful view." That one?

206
00:12:04,216 --> 00:12:06,416
<i>I think that's the power of a beautiful view.</i>

207
00:12:06,416 --> 00:12:08,140
My own little views that give me energy

208
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:12,124
when I'm tired and help me
get moving again when I stop.

209
00:12:12,124 --> 00:12:15,816
Have you ever had a beautiful moment
like that in your life, Bo Na?

210
00:12:21,056 --> 00:12:23,252
Oh, I'm sorry.

211
00:12:23,252 --> 00:12:25,616
That's a beautiful thing to say.

212
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:30,416
They must have a very romantic,
almost girlish sensibility.

213
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,516
I guess so.

214
00:12:31,516 --> 00:12:35,249
But their way of talking
is so blunt, like a guy.

215
00:12:49,183 --> 00:12:52,749
[Ok's Flower Shop]

216
00:12:56,808 --> 00:13:00,580
So that pickpocket wasn't caught
until a full year later.

217
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:02,888
Huh? But why is he still in here?

218
00:13:02,888 --> 00:13:06,149
Because he was charged with
aggravated assault and fleeing.

219
00:13:12,216 --> 00:13:15,816
Prison food must suit you well.
You look healthy.

220
00:13:20,532 --> 00:13:22,408
It's been a while.

221
00:13:22,408 --> 00:13:24,876
So, why are you here now,
after all this time?

222
00:13:24,876 --> 00:13:27,216
Here to grab me by the collar again?

223
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,436
Your friend is safe and sound, huh?

224
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:34,840
Yeah, he's doing fine.

225
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,332
I just came to ask you something.

226
00:13:36,332 --> 00:13:38,024
That day you mugged him.

227
00:13:38,024 --> 00:13:41,716
I told you everything about the day.
What else do you want?

228
00:13:45,249 --> 00:13:47,464
Your friend kept chasing me,

229
00:13:47,464 --> 00:13:50,483
so I hit him with a fire extinguisher
to knock him out...

230
00:13:51,116 --> 00:13:52,668
But I hit him too hard.

231
00:13:52,668 --> 00:13:55,116
I know all that. What happens next?

232
00:13:55,116 --> 00:13:56,500
After you hit him.

233
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,492
So, I ran outside.

234
00:13:58,492 --> 00:13:59,964
You left through the first-floor lobby?

235
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:02,080
Of course, I left through
the first floor. Where else?

236
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:05,504
Did you see anyone while you were
making your way out?

237
00:14:05,504 --> 00:14:07,480
See what?

238
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,649
It was dark and completely empty.

239
00:14:11,632 --> 00:14:13,300
Wait.

240
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:17,483
Come to think of it,
there may have been someone.

241
00:14:18,108 --> 00:14:20,340
There was?

242
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:21,352
Who?

243
00:14:21,352 --> 00:14:24,052
Oh, but can I say I saw someone?

244
00:14:24,052 --> 00:14:25,524
It wasn't actually inside the building.

245
00:14:25,524 --> 00:14:29,416
Inside or outside the building, who was it?

246
00:14:29,416 --> 00:14:31,283
A woman.

247
00:14:40,249 --> 00:14:42,116
[King Tower]

248
00:14:43,512 --> 00:14:48,183
<i>At the time Tae Seong entered the King Tower
building chasing the pickpocket,</i>

249
00:14:49,116 --> 00:14:53,249
<i>Kingfisher was on the roof of that building.</i>

250
00:15:14,016 --> 00:15:17,120
<i>The victim was on the phone
with a friend at a hotel across the street.</i>

251
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:19,714
- <i>During the call,</i>
- So what? Hello?

252
00:15:19,714 --> 00:15:22,349
<i>South Korea scored their first goal,</i>

253
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,584
<i>and moments later,
he was shot dead by a sniper.</i>

254
00:15:25,584 --> 00:15:28,783
<i>It was 11:02 PM.</i>

255
00:15:33,024 --> 00:15:37,016
<i>It would have taken just over
a minute to walk quickly from the rooftop</i>

256
00:15:37,016 --> 00:15:39,040
<i>down to the fifth floor.</i>

257
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:42,983
<i>If she found Tae Seong
collapsed here at that time...</i>

258
00:15:45,764 --> 00:15:51,152
The records show the emergency call
came in at 11:07 PM.

259
00:15:51,152 --> 00:15:54,680
It was a long time ago,
but do you remember the caller's voice?

260
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:56,728
Their way of speaking or accent?

261
00:15:56,728 --> 00:15:59,049
Well, it was a long time ago...

262
00:15:59,049 --> 00:16:02,464
I just remember that she sounded
like a young woman.

263
00:16:02,464 --> 00:16:06,676
I think she briefly stated what happened
and hung up right away.

264
00:16:06,676 --> 00:16:10,716
Oh, I remember someone shouting nearby
just before the call came in.

265
00:16:10,716 --> 00:16:13,628
I think Korea had just scored
and taken the lead?

266
00:16:13,628 --> 00:16:18,264
<i>Korea scored its second goal at 11:06 PM.</i>

267
00:16:18,264 --> 00:16:21,549
<i>The ambulance call
came in immediately afterward.</i>

268
00:16:28,583 --> 00:16:31,283
[Gate 3]

269
00:16:35,083 --> 00:16:39,349
If we open the first-floor restroom
to the public, it gets insanely dirty.

270
00:16:39,349 --> 00:16:44,368
<i>So the owner ordered us to lock
all the doors and said no one gets in.</i>

271
00:16:44,368 --> 00:16:50,516
But then some lunatic opened one of
the first-floor doors without me knowing.

272
00:17:02,536 --> 00:17:06,649
<i>It took roughly two minutes to get
from the fifth-floor stairs to outside.</i>

273
00:17:06,649 --> 00:17:12,316
<i>And right here,
the pickpocket said he saw a woman.</i>

274
00:17:12,316 --> 00:17:14,016
<i>A woman?</i>

275
00:17:14,648 --> 00:17:17,424
- Are you sure?
- I told you, yes.

276
00:17:17,424 --> 00:17:20,388
It's not like I can't tell
a man from a woman.

277
00:17:20,388 --> 00:17:23,456
[Parking Lot Entrance]
<i>It was my first time hitting someone,</i>

278
00:17:23,456 --> 00:17:25,049
<i>so I was nervous about what would happen</i>

279
00:17:25,049 --> 00:17:28,788
<i>and was hanging around nearby
to keep an eye on things.</i>

280
00:17:28,788 --> 00:17:31,920
<i>Then I saw a woman come out of the building.</i>

281
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:35,916
<i>It was too dark to see her face.
I only saw her from behind.</i>

282
00:17:35,916 --> 00:17:42,076
She was wearing a red T-shirt
and some kind of pointed headband.

283
00:17:42,076 --> 00:17:45,916
I figured the Red Devil, a World Cup fan,
had just been to the bathroom.

284
00:17:45,916 --> 00:17:47,849
The Red Devil?

285
00:17:49,316 --> 00:17:50,349
Was she alone?

286
00:17:50,349 --> 00:17:52,068
Yes, she was alone.

287
00:17:52,068 --> 00:17:55,949
Do you remember anything else?
Like her build or hairstyle.

288
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:58,083
She was pretty tall...

289
00:17:58,884 --> 00:18:01,349
and seemed slender.

290
00:18:01,984 --> 00:18:03,932
I think she had short hair.

291
00:18:03,932 --> 00:18:06,016
[Headband, Red Devil]
Short hair...

292
00:18:06,016 --> 00:18:07,260
No, maybe it was tied back?

293
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:09,987
Was she carrying or wearing anything else?

294
00:18:09,987 --> 00:18:14,948
Oh, right. She had a big bag
slung over her shoulder.

295
00:18:14,948 --> 00:18:18,416
About this big?

296
00:18:19,764 --> 00:18:20,788
She was tall...

297
00:18:20,788 --> 00:18:22,083
What time did you see her?

298
00:18:22,083 --> 00:18:24,810
Come on, how would I remember that?

299
00:18:24,810 --> 00:18:29,349
Oh, but when she came out,
I think Korea scored a goal or something.

300
00:18:29,349 --> 00:18:32,516
Everyone was cheering like crazy

301
00:18:32,516 --> 00:18:34,312
<i>and making a huge commotion.</i>

302
00:18:34,312 --> 00:18:37,624
<i>Around 11:10 PM, give or take.</i>

303
00:18:37,624 --> 00:18:40,249
<i>Given the route and timing,</i>

304
00:18:40,249 --> 00:18:43,952
<i>it's highly likely that
the woman who reported Tae Seong</i>

305
00:18:43,952 --> 00:18:46,249
<i>and the woman seen by the pickpocket
were the same person.</i>

306
00:18:46,988 --> 00:18:48,796
<i>Then...</i>

307
00:18:48,796 --> 00:18:53,183
Kingfisher is a tall,

308
00:18:53,183 --> 00:18:56,916
<i>well-built young man.</i>

309
00:19:05,516 --> 00:19:09,549
[Mr. Tiger]

310
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,649
<i>Why aren't you answering again?</i>

311
00:19:19,224 --> 00:19:20,924
<i>Busy.</i>

312
00:19:21,868 --> 00:19:23,583
<i>Call me when you're free.</i>

313
00:19:24,444 --> 00:19:26,144
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

314
00:19:28,016 --> 00:19:29,097
[- What are you doing tonight?
- Busy.]

315
00:19:29,097 --> 00:19:30,149
[- What are you up to this weekend?
- Busy.]

316
00:19:30,149 --> 00:19:32,216
[- Gaming cafe today? What are you doing?
- Busy.]

317
00:19:35,904 --> 00:19:38,049
I usually just come here to deliver chicken.

318
00:19:38,049 --> 00:19:40,483
This is the first time I've come here
for something like this.

319
00:19:40,483 --> 00:19:45,384
I somehow ended up helping catch
criminals too. It's a pretty strange feeling.

320
00:19:45,384 --> 00:19:47,500
You deliver chicken?

321
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:51,116
Seong Hun orders chicken
from our place all the time.

322
00:19:51,116 --> 00:19:54,149
Even though I keep telling him
to order from somewhere nearby,

323
00:19:54,149 --> 00:19:57,716
he says there aren't
any chicken places around here.

324
00:19:57,716 --> 00:20:01,316
How do you know him?

325
00:20:02,249 --> 00:20:04,104
We met at a judo gym in elementary school.

326
00:20:04,104 --> 00:20:06,749
On his first day, he underestimated me
and picked a fight,

327
00:20:06,749 --> 00:20:08,632
so I threw him in one move.

328
00:20:08,632 --> 00:20:11,500
I guess he was embarrassed,
so he asked me to keep it a secret.

329
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,612
So I suggested we become friends instead.

330
00:20:13,612 --> 00:20:16,616
He's actually two years older than me.

331
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,708
Se Ah.

332
00:20:23,677 --> 00:20:25,304
Shall we meet again?

333
00:20:25,304 --> 00:20:27,049
You startled me.

334
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,328
Why?

335
00:20:30,328 --> 00:20:33,824
I've started wanting to know
what kind of person you are.

336
00:20:33,824 --> 00:20:35,952
Really?

337
00:20:35,952 --> 00:20:38,912
Yes, I'd love to! Let's meet!

338
00:20:38,912 --> 00:20:41,949
Next time, just the two of us.

339
00:20:43,348 --> 00:20:45,916
Since he seems to have feelings for you.

340
00:20:51,748 --> 00:20:55,296
No way! That's ridiculous.

341
00:20:55,296 --> 00:20:57,321
We've known each other long enough

342
00:20:57,321 --> 00:20:59,416
to have seen each other
at our best and worst.

343
00:20:59,416 --> 00:21:02,020
Oh, come on. No, no.

344
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:04,216
Come on, no chance!

345
00:21:07,576 --> 00:21:09,849
Oh, dear. I'm home from school.

346
00:21:09,849 --> 00:21:11,549
You're back?

347
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:15,632
Why's Mom so happy today?

348
00:21:15,632 --> 00:21:16,632
Oh, so happy!

349
00:21:16,632 --> 00:21:19,049
Today's the day she gets
her savings out. Five years' worth.

350
00:21:19,049 --> 00:21:21,516
Wow, today's the day?

351
00:21:21,516 --> 00:21:24,876
No wonder you're happy with
a big chunk of money coming in.

352
00:21:24,876 --> 00:21:26,483
What, is she paying off the loan?

353
00:21:26,483 --> 00:21:28,044
She said she was
planning to redo the kitchen.

354
00:21:28,044 --> 00:21:30,000
The fryer is pretty old.

355
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,816
Hey, this is the last delivery, isn't it?

356
00:21:32,816 --> 00:21:34,184
Yeah, the last one.

357
00:21:34,184 --> 00:21:36,736
Okay, I'll do it, and...

358
00:21:36,736 --> 00:21:37,772
What time is it now?

359
00:21:37,772 --> 00:21:42,596
Oh, my, I'll stop by the bank,
go grocery shopping, and head straight home.

360
00:21:42,596 --> 00:21:46,349
So come home later.
Let's wrap up early today.

361
00:21:46,349 --> 00:21:47,349
Oh, dear.

362
00:21:47,349 --> 00:21:49,492
What? Are we having
something delicious today?

363
00:21:49,492 --> 00:21:50,924
Then I'll have beef.

364
00:21:50,924 --> 00:21:53,372
Beef?

365
00:21:53,372 --> 00:21:55,680
- Sure, let's have it.
- Wow!

366
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:56,797
Goodness.

367
00:21:56,797 --> 00:21:59,616
Tell Tae Seong's family to come if they can.

368
00:22:01,136 --> 00:22:02,808
Mom, buy lots of meat.

369
00:22:02,808 --> 00:22:05,483
- Korean beef!
- See you later.

370
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:10,283
Looks like she's planning to
apologize with beef.

371
00:22:11,116 --> 00:22:13,956
Hey, you go handle this one.
Bunhong Apartments.

372
00:22:13,956 --> 00:22:17,380
Come on, I told you to call a courier!

373
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:19,600
Hey, Seong Hun stopped by yesterday.

374
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:21,240
Huh? What? Why?

375
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:23,004
Why else? He came to buy chicken.

376
00:22:23,004 --> 00:22:25,931
He asked if something happened because
he hasn't been able to reach you lately.

377
00:22:25,931 --> 00:22:27,049
Did you two have a fight?

378
00:22:27,049 --> 00:22:29,896
Come on, we're not kids.

379
00:22:29,896 --> 00:22:32,504
Where? Bunhong Apartments? I'm going!

380
00:22:32,504 --> 00:22:34,532
Hey, you need the building and unit number!

381
00:22:34,532 --> 00:22:36,849
Building 108, Unit 504!

382
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,916
Oh.

383
00:22:44,916 --> 00:22:45,916
Hello?

384
00:22:45,916 --> 00:22:48,257
<i>Hello, is this Ms. Ok Seon Ja?</i>

385
00:22:48,257 --> 00:22:49,588
Yes. Who is this?

386
00:22:49,588 --> 00:22:52,575
<i>I'm Manager Kim Mi So
from the Korea Inclusive Finance Agency,</i>

387
00:22:52,575 --> 00:22:53,996
<i>a government-affiliated institution.</i>

388
00:22:53,996 --> 00:22:58,511
<i>I'm calling because you've been
selected for a low-interest loan program.</i>

389
00:22:58,511 --> 00:23:02,896
Me? Why? I don't need a loan.

390
00:23:02,896 --> 00:23:04,649
<i>It's a loan program designed for</i>

391
00:23:04,649 --> 00:23:09,240
<i>self-employed business owners
with interest rates around 0.8%.</i>

392
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:11,092
0.8%?

393
00:23:11,092 --> 00:23:13,016
<i>Yes, according to our records,</i>

394
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:16,748
<i>you previously took out a loan
with Haneop Bank.</i>

395
00:23:16,748 --> 00:23:19,964
Oh, yes. I do. That was...

396
00:23:19,964 --> 00:23:21,996
I think it was around 4.2%?

397
00:23:21,996 --> 00:23:23,921
<i>Our rates are much lower,</i>

398
00:23:23,921 --> 00:23:26,649
<i>so a lot of people move their loans here
to save on interest.</i>

399
00:23:26,649 --> 00:23:29,149
<i>Some even save a million won a month.</i>

400
00:23:29,149 --> 00:23:30,460
As much as a million won?

401
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:33,048
<i>Yes, a million won.</i>

402
00:23:33,048 --> 00:23:34,896
Oh, my, what?

403
00:23:34,896 --> 00:23:36,000
Wow, that's great.

404
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,105
<i>But there's just one condition.</i>

405
00:23:38,105 --> 00:23:42,449
<i>You have to pay off your
existing loan first to use ours.</i>

406
00:23:42,449 --> 00:23:45,283
<i>Would you be interested?</i>

407
00:23:45,283 --> 00:23:47,649
Well, I'm not sure...

408
00:23:47,649 --> 00:23:50,116
I'll check with the kids first.

409
00:23:50,116 --> 00:23:53,616
<i>But the deadline is today,
so if you're not interested,</i>

410
00:23:53,616 --> 00:23:55,676
<i>I need to contact the next person right away.</i>

411
00:23:55,676 --> 00:23:59,116
No, wait.

412
00:24:01,316 --> 00:24:04,356
I'll do it! What do I need to do?

413
00:24:04,356 --> 00:24:07,988
<i>You need to repay the loan by today.
Can you pay back the loan today?</i>

414
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,716
What?

415
00:24:11,132 --> 00:24:14,280
I happen to have the money.

416
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:16,717
But the bank is closed right now.

417
00:24:16,717 --> 00:24:21,483
<i>Then I'll connect you with a Haneop Bank
branch partnered with our agency.</i>

418
00:24:24,252 --> 00:24:25,952
[Financial Fraud Prevention
Questionnaire Page, No]

419
00:24:42,701 --> 00:24:44,816
Oh, let's go.

420
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:46,716
Yeah. Honey, did you hear?

421
00:24:46,716 --> 00:24:49,680
Mom wants to have a beef feast.
When are you done?

422
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:53,080
I'm out reporting, but it shouldn't
take long. I'll come as soon as I'm done.

423
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:55,083
<i>Okay, see you later.</i>

424
00:25:10,149 --> 00:25:11,224
[Ok's Flower Shop]

425
00:25:11,224 --> 00:25:13,783
- Then I'll get going.
- Thank you.

426
00:25:26,949 --> 00:25:29,416
[Ok's Flower Shop]

427
00:25:30,316 --> 00:25:32,712
[Ok's Flower Shop]

428
00:25:32,712 --> 00:25:35,476
So this place has been here all along?

429
00:25:35,476 --> 00:25:36,642
Welcome!

430
00:25:36,642 --> 00:25:38,342
Hello.

431
00:25:40,504 --> 00:25:43,404
I didn't know there was such a pretty
flower shop in our neighborhood.

432
00:25:43,404 --> 00:25:46,536
Oh, you live nearby.

433
00:25:46,536 --> 00:25:49,776
People who mostly drive around
could easily miss it.

434
00:25:49,776 --> 00:25:53,500
Right. Men don't usually
pay much attention to flowers.

435
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:56,656
So I guess most of your customers
are women who live nearby.

436
00:25:56,656 --> 00:25:57,749
Why?

437
00:25:57,749 --> 00:26:02,792
Lots of men come in to buy flowers
for their wives or girlfriends.

438
00:26:02,792 --> 00:26:04,249
I see.

439
00:26:04,249 --> 00:26:06,416
- Can I look around...
- Yes.

440
00:26:16,048 --> 00:26:19,383
Are you looking for a particular flower?

441
00:26:20,472 --> 00:26:23,082
What's the meaning of this flower?

442
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,284
Sunflowers?

443
00:26:24,284 --> 00:26:27,283
They stand for hope, positivity, and support.

444
00:26:27,283 --> 00:26:31,638
People often give them
as congratulatory gifts or get-well gifts.

445
00:26:31,638 --> 00:26:33,732
It also means purifying
the dark energy in the home

446
00:26:33,732 --> 00:26:37,084
and filling it with bright, positive energy.

447
00:26:37,084 --> 00:26:39,116
I see. That's what it means.

448
00:26:41,135 --> 00:26:42,835
Well...

449
00:26:44,748 --> 00:26:49,483
Actually, I came to ask you something.

450
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:51,960
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]

451
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:56,616
Could you tell me anything about the person
who sends flowers to Yeon Cheol?

452
00:26:56,616 --> 00:26:58,732
Yeon Cheol...

453
00:26:58,732 --> 00:27:02,075
- Oh, the kid at the welfare center?
- Yes.

454
00:27:02,075 --> 00:27:05,683
Well, I just take the orders
and deliver the flowers.

455
00:27:07,329 --> 00:27:09,000
What about the flower meanings?

456
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:12,264
I heard they send a card
explaining them every time.

457
00:27:12,264 --> 00:27:13,552
That was me.

458
00:27:13,552 --> 00:27:15,948
They never gave me
a specific message to pass along,

459
00:27:15,948 --> 00:27:18,916
and sending flowers
with nothing at all felt a little empty.

460
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:22,964
But one of the staff members remembered
what was written on the first card.

461
00:27:22,964 --> 00:27:24,428
Then, could that have been...

462
00:27:24,428 --> 00:27:27,892
The first card...
I suppose it was probably that.

463
00:27:27,892 --> 00:27:30,176
Do you remember what you wrote?

464
00:27:30,176 --> 00:27:33,349
Well, what was it again?

465
00:27:34,028 --> 00:27:37,280
<i>"I hope you find your own beautiful view."</i>

466
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:39,044
<i>That was all it said.</i>

467
00:27:39,044 --> 00:27:42,704
"I hope you always smile
as brightly as a flower."

468
00:27:42,704 --> 00:27:45,320
Oh, right. That's what I wrote.

469
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:48,283
Since they were for a child, after all.

470
00:27:55,752 --> 00:27:57,452
Oh, hello.

471
00:27:59,084 --> 00:28:03,383
I'm Assistant Manager Kwon Dong Hun
from Haneop Bank's Gwanghwamun branch.

472
00:28:03,383 --> 00:28:05,088
[Assistant Manager Kwon Dong Hun]

473
00:28:05,088 --> 00:28:07,536
But how am I supposed to know you're really

474
00:28:07,536 --> 00:28:09,452
with the bank from just a business card?

475
00:28:09,452 --> 00:28:12,192
It's just that the world is
so full of scams these days.

476
00:28:12,192 --> 00:28:14,164
Of course, completely understandable.

477
00:28:14,164 --> 00:28:19,408
Alright, here's my bank ID card.

478
00:28:19,408 --> 00:28:23,804
- These are the loan repayment documents.
- Oh, oh... Yes.

479
00:28:23,804 --> 00:28:27,416
Take your time reading them,
and then sign here.

480
00:28:28,824 --> 00:28:30,552
[Loan Repayment]
Oh, right. This is right.

481
00:28:30,552 --> 00:28:36,249
- Oh, okay, just a moment.
- Sure, take your time.

482
00:28:43,956 --> 00:28:46,720
- I've signed this part.
- Oh, yes.

483
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,420
By the way...

484
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:52,288
this will pay off my loan, right?

485
00:28:52,288 --> 00:28:53,416
Of course.

486
00:28:53,416 --> 00:28:57,048
You called the bank yourself, after all.

487
00:28:57,048 --> 00:28:59,048
Alright, then...

488
00:28:59,048 --> 00:29:00,748
Wait...

489
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:03,149
Well...

490
00:29:03,849 --> 00:29:06,083
Well, Ma'am.

491
00:29:06,083 --> 00:29:10,716
My team leader is actually
waiting for me and can't leave work yet.

492
00:29:11,588 --> 00:29:15,516
Oh, I'm so sorry.

493
00:29:15,516 --> 00:29:18,483
I'm so sorry. You're so busy,
couldn't even leave work,

494
00:29:18,483 --> 00:29:20,916
and still came all the way
to my home. Thank you.

495
00:29:20,916 --> 00:29:23,180
Oh, we're the ones who should thank you.

496
00:29:23,180 --> 00:29:25,565
- I'll make sure your money
- Yeah.

497
00:29:25,565 --> 00:29:27,652
gets safely transferred.

498
00:29:27,652 --> 00:29:31,716
Okay. Please take good care of it.

499
00:29:31,716 --> 00:29:32,949
- Yes.
- Please go inside.

500
00:29:32,949 --> 00:29:35,549
- Yes...
- Don't worry about a thing.

501
00:29:35,549 --> 00:29:36,849
Keep the money safe.

502
00:29:36,849 --> 00:29:38,064
- Go inside.
- Yes.

503
00:29:38,064 --> 00:29:40,116
- Call us again if you need anything.
- Okay.

504
00:29:49,316 --> 00:29:51,768
[Boss]

505
00:29:51,768 --> 00:29:54,588
Darn it, the old lady was so suspicious.

506
00:29:54,588 --> 00:29:57,276
Does she really think
that makes her look smart?

507
00:29:57,276 --> 00:29:59,668
Sure, I made it back safe and sound.

508
00:29:59,668 --> 00:30:02,549
But the commission is 10%, right?

509
00:30:04,092 --> 00:30:06,849
Yes. I'll meet you there.

510
00:30:08,683 --> 00:30:11,532
- Let's go.
- Oh, my.

511
00:30:11,532 --> 00:30:13,400
Hello.

512
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:15,383
Oh, hey there.

513
00:30:16,836 --> 00:30:19,192
- Can we get off?
- Oh, sure.

514
00:30:19,192 --> 00:30:21,083
- Yes, sorry.
- Let's go, Yul.

515
00:30:24,336 --> 00:30:26,036
Oh, yeah.

516
00:30:27,444 --> 00:30:29,968
- Let's go.
- Whoa.

517
00:30:30,568 --> 00:30:33,144
Why did I just get a chill down my spine?

518
00:30:33,144 --> 00:30:35,444
What, is something wrong?

519
00:30:35,444 --> 00:30:37,052
- Huh?
- Grandma!

520
00:30:37,052 --> 00:30:39,583
Oh, my baby is here?

521
00:30:39,583 --> 00:30:42,188
Mother, did someone come by?

522
00:30:42,188 --> 00:30:43,724
Yeah, a bank employee.

523
00:30:43,724 --> 00:30:45,552
Oh, the young man worked so hard.

524
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,992
He couldn't even leave work
and came all the way to a customer's house.

525
00:30:47,992 --> 00:30:49,180
A bank employee?

526
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:51,124
Yeah.

527
00:30:51,124 --> 00:30:53,116
Mother, did you give him the money?

528
00:30:53,116 --> 00:30:54,288
Of course, I did.

529
00:30:54,288 --> 00:30:56,188
He came to collect the loan repayment.

530
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:58,283
The savings payout I got today...

531
00:30:59,704 --> 00:31:01,956
Why? What's wrong?

532
00:31:01,956 --> 00:31:04,196
Mother, this really
looks like voice phishing.

533
00:31:04,196 --> 00:31:06,216
- Stay home with Yul. Okay?
- What?

534
00:31:06,849 --> 00:31:08,549
What?

535
00:31:09,776 --> 00:31:11,476
Oh, my God!

536
00:31:12,776 --> 00:31:15,283
What do I do?

537
00:31:28,364 --> 00:31:29,834
Oh, seriously.

538
00:31:32,501 --> 00:31:33,620
Oh, she's...

539
00:31:33,620 --> 00:31:35,540
What is she going to do?

540
00:31:35,540 --> 00:31:37,236
What?

541
00:31:37,236 --> 00:31:39,201
Huh? That woman from earlier.

542
00:31:39,201 --> 00:31:40,901
Darn it.

543
00:31:41,684 --> 00:31:42,872
You, get out.

544
00:31:42,872 --> 00:31:46,045
What? Did she figure me out?

545
00:31:46,045 --> 00:31:47,783
Darn it!

546
00:31:56,847 --> 00:31:58,224
Oh! Darn it!

547
00:31:58,224 --> 00:32:00,680
Has that punk lost her mind?

548
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:02,516
You want to play, huh?

549
00:32:13,828 --> 00:32:15,528
Oh, that startled me!

550
00:32:16,916 --> 00:32:19,249
Oh, my!

551
00:32:23,683 --> 00:32:24,683
Oh, my heart.

552
00:32:24,683 --> 00:32:27,231
Wait, what did I just see?

553
00:32:27,231 --> 00:32:30,516
- <i>Yes, Ms. Yoo.</i>
- Can you run a license plate for me?

554
00:32:30,516 --> 00:32:31,800
- Se Ah!
- Bo Na!

555
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:32,868
Where are you going?

556
00:32:32,868 --> 00:32:34,896
I need to catch that car.
It's voice phishing.

557
00:32:34,896 --> 00:32:37,108
What? Voice phishing?

558
00:32:37,108 --> 00:32:38,340
T-T-That one over there?

559
00:32:38,340 --> 00:32:39,849
Yeah.

560
00:32:39,849 --> 00:32:41,016
Assistant Manager Ki, I've got this.

561
00:32:41,016 --> 00:32:42,716
Wait, Ms. Yoo...

562
00:32:49,085 --> 00:32:50,785
Voice phishing?

563
00:32:52,780 --> 00:32:54,949
Then those two women...

564
00:32:56,742 --> 00:32:58,442
Wow.

565
00:32:59,536 --> 00:33:02,049
Of all the people to mess with...

566
00:33:03,583 --> 00:33:06,896
But Bo Na, why are you chasing him?

567
00:33:06,896 --> 00:33:08,704
Who's the victim?

568
00:33:08,704 --> 00:33:11,416
Mother. He ran off with her savings.

569
00:33:11,416 --> 00:33:13,608
What? That crazy punk!

570
00:33:13,608 --> 00:33:15,449
Hold on tight, Bo Na!

571
00:33:31,956 --> 00:33:33,288
Se Ah, drop me off over there.

572
00:33:33,288 --> 00:33:34,908
What? Why?

573
00:33:34,908 --> 00:33:36,852
Hurry.

574
00:33:36,852 --> 00:33:39,383
What are you planning to do?

575
00:33:40,952 --> 00:33:42,349
I have to get Mother's money back.

576
00:33:42,349 --> 00:33:43,816
I'll see you at home. I'm going.

577
00:33:43,816 --> 00:33:45,263
You're going alone?

578
00:33:45,263 --> 00:33:47,816
Bo Na, please be careful.

579
00:33:48,604 --> 00:33:50,483
I'm going to get you.

580
00:34:18,578 --> 00:34:20,320
Darn it.

581
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:22,783
Man, I've been running a lot lately.

582
00:34:35,644 --> 00:34:37,349
Why are you following me?

583
00:34:54,849 --> 00:34:56,816
- Are you okay?
- Are you all right?

584
00:35:29,449 --> 00:35:31,697
What?

585
00:35:31,697 --> 00:35:34,097
Oh, my! Darn it!

586
00:35:45,850 --> 00:35:48,248
What? Are you police?

587
00:35:48,248 --> 00:35:49,820
Someone scarier than the police.

588
00:35:49,820 --> 00:35:51,728
Darn it!

589
00:35:51,728 --> 00:35:56,549
You're not even a cop, lady,
but you've seriously got no fear.

590
00:35:57,336 --> 00:35:58,528
What are you going to do?

591
00:35:58,528 --> 00:36:01,880
There's no one around,
and there aren't any CCTV cameras either.

592
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:03,872
Is that so?

593
00:36:03,872 --> 00:36:05,656
Perfect. Get up.

594
00:36:05,656 --> 00:36:07,356
What?

595
00:36:08,216 --> 00:36:10,883
[Seoul Nambu Police Station]

596
00:36:14,244 --> 00:36:16,096
Can we get Mother's money back right away?

597
00:36:16,096 --> 00:36:17,156
I'm worried she might collapse.

598
00:36:17,156 --> 00:36:18,156
Ms. Bo Na!

599
00:36:18,156 --> 00:36:20,516
- Kwon Se Ah!
- Mr. Dong Jin.

600
00:36:20,516 --> 00:36:21,568
Oh, hello.

601
00:36:21,568 --> 00:36:23,616
Ms. Bo Na, are you alright?

602
00:36:23,616 --> 00:36:24,649
Yes, I'm fine.

603
00:36:24,649 --> 00:36:26,824
You were busy.
What brought you all the way here?

604
00:36:26,824 --> 00:36:29,420
Why did you chase them? It was dangerous.
You weren't hurt, were you?

605
00:36:29,420 --> 00:36:30,783
I'm fine.

606
00:36:30,783 --> 00:36:32,612
Thank you for worrying about me.

607
00:36:32,612 --> 00:36:33,752
- Oh, Mr. Lee.
- Sorry.

608
00:36:33,752 --> 00:36:35,004
Do you know her?

609
00:36:35,004 --> 00:36:37,072
Yeah, she's family.

610
00:36:37,072 --> 00:36:39,556
What? Family?

611
00:36:39,556 --> 00:36:40,956
Oh, what about the voice-phishing scammers?

612
00:36:40,956 --> 00:36:42,983
Oh, they're over there.

613
00:36:44,481 --> 00:36:45,600
What's wrong with those punks?

614
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:47,132
Looks like they fell and rolled around

615
00:36:47,132 --> 00:36:50,264
while trying to get away from these ladies.

616
00:36:50,264 --> 00:36:52,256
No, that's not what happened!

617
00:36:52,256 --> 00:36:55,716
That wretch in red threw me
with a hip toss! Three times, even!

618
00:36:55,716 --> 00:36:58,788
And that lady hit me with a Coke,

619
00:36:58,788 --> 00:37:01,356
kicked me here, and kneed me here. Look!

620
00:37:01,356 --> 00:37:02,452
A knee kick?

621
00:37:02,452 --> 00:37:05,483
Seriously, they were fighting
among themselves and ended up falling over.

622
00:37:05,483 --> 00:37:07,183
Wow, that's pretty funny, huh?

623
00:37:07,183 --> 00:37:10,856
When can we get Mother's money back...

624
00:37:10,856 --> 00:37:13,549
Well, it takes a little longer because
we have to go through that procedure.

625
00:37:13,549 --> 00:37:14,652
- Really?
- Even after being caught...

626
00:37:14,652 --> 00:37:17,708
These guys still haven't come to
their senses. They're still talking nonsense.

627
00:37:17,708 --> 00:37:19,483
Looks like it. Hey, you punk. Come here!

628
00:37:19,483 --> 00:37:22,116
What, "that wretch"?
Who are you calling a wretch?

629
00:37:22,116 --> 00:37:23,816
Hey, get that mouth over here.

630
00:37:23,816 --> 00:37:26,776
- I'll kill you if I get in there.
- So cool.

631
00:37:26,776 --> 00:37:28,349
Honey!

632
00:37:28,349 --> 00:37:29,676
- Goodness, dear!
- Mother.

633
00:37:29,676 --> 00:37:31,012
Mom, Tae Seong!

634
00:37:31,012 --> 00:37:32,880
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

635
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:35,520
I'm perfectly fine, honey. Don't worry.

636
00:37:35,520 --> 00:37:37,149
Are you really okay?

637
00:37:37,149 --> 00:37:38,728
I'm perfectly fine, really.

638
00:37:38,728 --> 00:37:40,424
Oh, jeez.

639
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:43,652
My money! Sir, what about my money?

640
00:37:43,652 --> 00:37:47,516
We'll return it to you after the procedures,
so don't worry too much.

641
00:37:47,516 --> 00:37:49,884
Oh, thank goodness.

642
00:37:49,884 --> 00:37:52,849
That money means everything to me.

643
00:37:52,849 --> 00:37:55,516
It's usually hard to get your money back
once you've been scammed.

644
00:37:55,516 --> 00:37:58,449
These two ladies really
did something incredible.

645
00:37:58,449 --> 00:38:00,283
- Why...
- Why did you even chase after him?

646
00:38:00,283 --> 00:38:02,536
You should've called the police.

647
00:38:02,536 --> 00:38:04,101
Do you have any idea how scared I was?

648
00:38:04,101 --> 00:38:06,349
- I just happened to see it.
- Excuse me, Tae Seong.

649
00:38:06,349 --> 00:38:09,112
Can't you see your one
and only little sister here?

650
00:38:09,112 --> 00:38:10,720
Of course, you're fine.

651
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,181
- Why are you saying that?
- Why would you do something

652
00:38:12,181 --> 00:38:14,768
- so dangerous...
- Show a little more heartfelt concern!

653
00:38:14,768 --> 00:38:16,712
I have absolute faith in your well-being.

654
00:38:16,712 --> 00:38:18,749
- Oh, seriously...
- Stop having so much faith in me!

655
00:38:19,384 --> 00:38:20,564
Why?

656
00:38:21,428 --> 00:38:23,768
Why does getting my own money back
have to involve

657
00:38:23,768 --> 00:38:25,736
- such complicated procedures?
- Tell me about it.

658
00:38:25,736 --> 00:38:28,183
Man, I'm back here again.

659
00:38:28,183 --> 00:38:29,954
Another criminal caught.

660
00:38:29,954 --> 00:38:32,516
- What a fulfilling day.
- Oh, dear.

661
00:38:33,712 --> 00:38:39,083
But even so, that's too much.
You didn't have to go that far.

662
00:38:39,992 --> 00:38:41,332
No.

663
00:38:41,332 --> 00:38:45,908
It's your hard-earned money, saved up
penny by penny from dawn to dusk.

664
00:38:45,908 --> 00:38:47,608
Of course, we had to get it back.

665
00:38:48,804 --> 00:38:53,749
Anyway, I'd have been
in serious trouble without you.

666
00:38:53,749 --> 00:38:55,483
Than...

667
00:38:56,172 --> 00:38:57,872
Than...

668
00:38:58,664 --> 00:39:00,364
Than...

669
00:39:01,492 --> 00:39:04,160
Then let's go get some meat.

670
00:39:04,160 --> 00:39:07,416
Is it really that hard to say thank you?

671
00:39:08,996 --> 00:39:10,568
Let's go, Se Ah.

672
00:39:10,568 --> 00:39:12,049
Mother, let's go together!

673
00:39:12,049 --> 00:39:14,872
Is that pride or just stubbornness?

674
00:39:14,872 --> 00:39:16,572
Kwon Se Ah!

675
00:39:22,952 --> 00:39:25,083
Are you seriously leaving
without saying goodbye?

676
00:39:32,556 --> 00:39:33,796
Why are you avoiding me?

677
00:39:33,796 --> 00:39:37,460
When did I? I'm not avoiding you.

678
00:39:37,460 --> 00:39:38,652
Did I do something wrong?

679
00:39:38,652 --> 00:39:40,328
No.

680
00:39:40,328 --> 00:39:44,483
It's not that you did anything wrong...

681
00:39:44,483 --> 00:39:46,648
Why are you trailing off like that?
That's not like you.

682
00:39:46,648 --> 00:39:48,980
Hey, just spit it out. What is it?

683
00:39:48,980 --> 00:39:51,449
Do you...

684
00:39:54,544 --> 00:39:56,632
Stop beating around the bush and just say it.

685
00:39:56,632 --> 00:39:57,892
What about me?

686
00:39:57,892 --> 00:39:59,749
Do you like me?

687
00:40:07,916 --> 00:40:11,549
Hey, that's why you...
You're seriously funny.

688
00:40:12,420 --> 00:40:14,952
Hey, what's so funny about that?

689
00:40:14,952 --> 00:40:16,364
Forget it if not!

690
00:40:16,364 --> 00:40:20,320
I was just asking
because I wondered. That's all.

691
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:23,249
Seriously, you drive me crazy.

692
00:40:26,616 --> 00:40:28,436
Oh, that's what it is!

693
00:40:28,436 --> 00:40:31,048
What? What is it?

694
00:40:31,048 --> 00:40:32,850
So that's why I've been like this lately,

695
00:40:32,850 --> 00:40:36,660
getting annoyed when I can't reach you,
wondering what you're doing,

696
00:40:36,660 --> 00:40:39,683
wanting to see your face
and hear your voice. Now I get it...

697
00:40:40,756 --> 00:40:42,849
What?

698
00:40:42,849 --> 00:40:45,149
Huh, you're right.

699
00:40:48,092 --> 00:40:49,916
I guess I do like you.

700
00:41:02,620 --> 00:41:06,149
I'll let you know when the results come out.
It'll take a few days.

701
00:41:08,020 --> 00:41:09,764
Thanks for coming, even though you're busy.

702
00:41:09,764 --> 00:41:11,388
Don't even mention it.

703
00:41:11,388 --> 00:41:14,083
It's your wife's matter. How could I not go?

704
00:41:16,184 --> 00:41:17,760
I guess married couples
really do start to look alike.

705
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:21,549
How did she have the guts
to chase them like that?

706
00:41:21,549 --> 00:41:24,916
She doesn't take after me.
She's always been fearless.

707
00:41:24,916 --> 00:41:27,436
I suppose she's different from you,
always getting stabbed in the back.

708
00:41:27,436 --> 00:41:28,568
Jeez, give me a break.

709
00:41:28,568 --> 00:41:32,416
Hey, Bo Na was the one
who hit him with a Coke bottle.

710
00:41:33,380 --> 00:41:34,483
What?

711
00:41:34,483 --> 00:41:39,049
Maybe Bo Na should be protecting you
instead of the other way around.

712
00:41:40,572 --> 00:41:42,832
Come on, I'm not that bad.

713
00:41:42,832 --> 00:41:44,532
Jeez.

714
00:41:46,972 --> 00:41:49,724
Actually, I wanted to ask you something.
Good timing.

715
00:41:49,724 --> 00:41:51,816
- Ask me something?
- Yeah.

716
00:41:54,660 --> 00:41:57,736
That man you said you saw.

717
00:41:57,736 --> 00:41:59,436
Kingfisher.

718
00:42:00,788 --> 00:42:02,316
Hey, don't talk about that until I say...

719
00:42:02,316 --> 00:42:04,016
Hear me out first.

720
00:42:05,639 --> 00:42:08,616
Isn't it possible you saw him wrong?

721
00:42:10,284 --> 00:42:13,460
Why do you assume I was wrong
before even hearing me out?

722
00:42:13,460 --> 00:42:15,608
I ask you a question,
and you answer with another question?

723
00:42:15,608 --> 00:42:16,936
Then next question.

724
00:42:16,936 --> 00:42:19,928
Eight years ago, during the World Cup
pickpocketing case,

725
00:42:19,928 --> 00:42:23,204
did you ever find the woman
who called an ambulance for you?

726
00:42:23,204 --> 00:42:26,064
How am I supposed to find someone
I couldn't find back then?

727
00:42:26,064 --> 00:42:29,749
If I'd found her, I'd have met her
long ago. She saved my life.

728
00:42:30,472 --> 00:42:31,800
But why are you suddenly asking about her?

729
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:33,896
There should be a recording
of her voice on your phone.

730
00:42:33,896 --> 00:42:35,916
Reporters usually have automatic
call recording turned on.

731
00:42:35,916 --> 00:42:37,116
Didn't you listen to it?

732
00:42:37,116 --> 00:42:40,340
Of course, I did. Right after I woke up.

733
00:42:40,340 --> 00:42:41,716
But how would listening to
her voice tell me who she is?

734
00:42:41,716 --> 00:42:45,892
Am I supposed to compare her voice
with every woman's in Korea?

735
00:42:45,892 --> 00:42:49,264
Do you still have that phone?

736
00:42:49,264 --> 00:42:50,840
The one from back then?

737
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:53,060
Yeah.

738
00:42:53,060 --> 00:42:56,156
I got rid of it ages ago. That was years ago.

739
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:58,783
Why are you looking for her anyway?

740
00:43:03,383 --> 00:43:09,249
She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.

741
00:43:09,940 --> 00:43:11,640
Or...

742
00:43:12,272 --> 00:43:14,383
she could even be Kingfisher herself.

743
00:43:15,348 --> 00:43:17,048
What?

744
00:43:17,772 --> 00:43:19,849
Tae Seong,

745
00:43:19,849 --> 00:43:23,048
stop withholding information
and confusing me.

746
00:43:23,048 --> 00:43:26,036
Otherwise, I'll send you
an official summons soon.

747
00:43:26,036 --> 00:43:29,149
You know I'm on the Kingfisher
task force now, right?

748
00:43:39,412 --> 00:43:41,156
Wow!

749
00:43:41,156 --> 00:43:44,668
The meat is really good today.
Where did you get it?

750
00:43:44,668 --> 00:43:47,170
It's Sangju beef. Sangju beef.

751
00:43:47,170 --> 00:43:52,983
I asked for the very best cut,
so eat as much as you want today.

752
00:43:52,983 --> 00:43:54,783
- Thank you.
- Okay!

753
00:43:56,252 --> 00:44:00,649
She was begging for beef all day.
Why isn't she eating?

754
00:44:00,649 --> 00:44:03,983
Leave her alone.
Maybe she's full without eating.

755
00:44:05,766 --> 00:44:07,260
What's wrong with him now?

756
00:44:07,260 --> 00:44:09,272
Hey, the meat's going to burn.

757
00:44:09,272 --> 00:44:10,983
Yeah.

758
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,883
Oh, flowers.

759
00:44:14,883 --> 00:44:16,532
Yul's mom bought them.

760
00:44:16,532 --> 00:44:19,949
That really brightens up the whole place.

761
00:44:21,552 --> 00:44:25,992
I got them at the flower shop up front
while I was coming here, Mother.

762
00:44:25,992 --> 00:44:29,949
I heard sunflowers cleanse
a home of negative energy

763
00:44:29,949 --> 00:44:33,149
and fill it with bright, positive energy.

764
00:44:34,340 --> 00:44:36,016
So that's what sunflowers mean.

765
00:44:36,016 --> 00:44:39,284
Seriously though, you're something else.

766
00:44:39,284 --> 00:44:43,316
How did you even think to chase
them down with your bare hands?

767
00:44:43,316 --> 00:44:45,516
Oh, well, that's...

768
00:44:46,408 --> 00:44:49,767
I think my body just reacted first.

769
00:44:49,767 --> 00:44:51,124
Right away!

770
00:44:51,124 --> 00:44:52,400
Especially with Se Ah there, I was just...

771
00:44:52,400 --> 00:44:54,100
That's impressive.

772
00:44:56,208 --> 00:44:58,044
Mother, the beef is so good.

773
00:44:58,044 --> 00:45:00,148
Yes, it's good.

774
00:45:00,148 --> 00:45:01,364
Eat up.

775
00:45:01,364 --> 00:45:05,483
Yul, have another bite.
It's not too hot, is it?

776
00:45:05,483 --> 00:45:07,160
Don't ever do that again.

777
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:09,716
Make sure you call the police first, okay?

778
00:45:09,716 --> 00:45:13,640
Whether your mom gets scammed or not,
you only care about your wife.

779
00:45:13,640 --> 00:45:15,240
Here you go again.

780
00:45:15,240 --> 00:45:17,400
Mom, are you proud of getting scammed?

781
00:45:17,400 --> 00:45:18,983
Wow. How could you fall for that?

782
00:45:18,983 --> 00:45:20,936
You're really rubbing salt in the wound.

783
00:45:20,936 --> 00:45:22,972
Let's see if you'd have fallen for it
if you got that call.

784
00:45:22,972 --> 00:45:24,349
I wouldn't.

785
00:45:24,349 --> 00:45:25,649
It's good.

786
00:45:25,649 --> 00:45:27,852
They couldn't find any other way
to get money? Huh?

787
00:45:27,852 --> 00:45:30,935
Steal someone's
hard-earned money like that? Huh?

788
00:45:30,935 --> 00:45:32,004
Wow, that's good enough.

789
00:45:32,004 --> 00:45:33,849
Try some rice too.

790
00:45:39,149 --> 00:45:41,516
This is really good.

791
00:45:42,336 --> 00:45:44,972
This is all cooked.

792
00:45:44,972 --> 00:45:50,783
Do you know how much effort I put in today?

793
00:46:05,692 --> 00:46:07,408
Honey! I'll do it.

794
00:46:07,408 --> 00:46:08,683
No, it's fine. Why are you doing this?

795
00:46:08,683 --> 00:46:09,683
- I'll do it.
- It'll only take a minute.

796
00:46:09,683 --> 00:46:10,688
- No, don't.
- Honey...

797
00:46:10,688 --> 00:46:12,416
Kwon Tae Seong!

798
00:46:17,468 --> 00:46:18,549
Mom, that's not it...

799
00:46:18,549 --> 00:46:22,416
The women did all the cooking,
so I'll at least do the dishes.

800
00:46:26,424 --> 00:46:29,476
There's a lot of grease, so use hot water.

801
00:46:29,476 --> 00:46:32,116
And rinse everything really well, okay?

802
00:46:40,912 --> 00:46:42,612
Here.

803
00:46:47,752 --> 00:46:50,283
Pull your clothes up a little.

804
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:52,880
Okay.

805
00:47:03,312 --> 00:47:05,483
- Pears cost more now.
- Mom, didn't you get any pears?

806
00:47:05,483 --> 00:47:07,576
I made time and got everything.

807
00:47:07,576 --> 00:47:11,249
Come on, Mom, I told you not to.

808
00:47:11,249 --> 00:47:14,283
- What?
- Hey!

809
00:47:14,283 --> 00:47:16,916
[Ok's Flower Shop]

810
00:47:32,783 --> 00:47:37,683
[Interviews with Kingfisher's
Victims' Associates]

811
00:47:48,728 --> 00:47:50,668
<i>Why are you looking for her anyway?</i>

812
00:47:50,668 --> 00:47:55,416
She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.

813
00:47:56,224 --> 00:47:59,683
<i>Or she could even be Kingfisher herself.</i>

814
00:48:20,176 --> 00:48:22,980
<i>Your husband stopped by the shop today.</i>

815
00:48:22,980 --> 00:48:25,204
<i>It seems he went looking for Cheol.</i>

816
00:48:25,204 --> 00:48:27,883
[Team Leader Bae]
<i>He asked about the flower sender.</i>

817
00:48:29,132 --> 00:48:33,449
<i>I gave him a vague answer,
but I thought you should know.</i>

818
00:48:44,483 --> 00:48:46,283
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

819
00:48:46,283 --> 00:48:49,149
The shooter was definitely just one person.

820
00:48:49,149 --> 00:48:50,624
But as you can see,

821
00:48:50,624 --> 00:48:53,044
there may have been an accomplice
involved in everything besides the shooting.

822
00:48:53,044 --> 00:48:57,816
We can't rule out the possibility of
a separate team operating independently.

823
00:48:57,816 --> 00:49:01,883
Kingfisher may have an organized
group of accomplices?

824
00:49:03,288 --> 00:49:04,560
That's plausible.

825
00:49:04,560 --> 00:49:05,624
Yes.

826
00:49:05,624 --> 00:49:07,916
If that's the case,
it's highly likely their methods

827
00:49:07,916 --> 00:49:10,476
go beyond simply carrying out sniper attacks,

828
00:49:10,476 --> 00:49:13,348
based on what we've uncovered so far.

829
00:49:13,348 --> 00:49:14,688
What is that supposed to mean?

830
00:49:14,688 --> 00:49:17,216
[Kingfisher Special Task Force]
If it's not a shooting, then what?

831
00:49:19,540 --> 00:49:20,784
[Analysis of Staged Accidental Deaths]
Pyo Kyu Cheol?

832
00:49:20,784 --> 00:49:22,472
Hey, he was shot and killed.

833
00:49:22,472 --> 00:49:25,404
I believe Kingfisher's side originally
planned to make it look like an accident,

834
00:49:25,404 --> 00:49:29,696
but some variable arose, forcing him
to finish the job with a shooting.

835
00:49:29,696 --> 00:49:31,396
What's the basis for that?

836
00:49:32,952 --> 00:49:36,276
We tracked eight serious child sex offenders

837
00:49:36,276 --> 00:49:39,548
from the past 15 years
since Kingfisher first appeared.

838
00:49:39,548 --> 00:49:44,028
All eight were confirmed
to have died in various accidents,

839
00:49:44,028 --> 00:49:47,244
car crashes, falls, electrocution,
drowning, and so on.

840
00:49:47,244 --> 00:49:50,204
While Kingfisher draws
attention with a shooting,

841
00:49:50,204 --> 00:49:54,783
a separate team eliminates criminals
by disguising their deaths as accidents?

842
00:49:56,340 --> 00:49:58,888
That's an interesting theory.

843
00:49:58,888 --> 00:50:00,564
Hey.

844
00:50:00,564 --> 00:50:02,549
Ms. Yoo, why are you doing this too?

845
00:50:03,468 --> 00:50:06,566
We tracked 20 serious criminals
who received relatively light sentences

846
00:50:06,566 --> 00:50:09,380
and were released over the past 15 years.

847
00:50:09,380 --> 00:50:12,316
11 were killed by Kingfisher's shootings,

848
00:50:12,316 --> 00:50:15,204
while 8 died in apparent accidents.

849
00:50:15,204 --> 00:50:17,260
And...

850
00:50:17,260 --> 00:50:19,516
the most recent victim, Hwang Cheol Beom.

851
00:50:19,516 --> 00:50:20,549
[Hwang Cheol Beom]

852
00:50:20,549 --> 00:50:23,584
He was so afraid of Kingfisher
that he voluntarily went back to prison,

853
00:50:23,584 --> 00:50:26,528
but he was found dead
inside the prison last week.

854
00:50:26,528 --> 00:50:29,249
The cause of death was cardiac arrest.

855
00:50:29,249 --> 00:50:30,824
Good grief.

856
00:50:30,824 --> 00:50:34,706
Some died in accidents. Others from illness.

857
00:50:34,706 --> 00:50:36,704
Are we a criminal obituary
task force or what?

858
00:50:36,704 --> 00:50:41,249
If 19 out of 20 are dead,

859
00:50:42,020 --> 00:50:43,720
who's the one that hasn't died yet?

860
00:50:47,672 --> 00:50:49,020
<i>Gu Jong Ryeol.</i>

861
00:50:49,020 --> 00:50:50,749
About two years ago,

862
00:50:50,749 --> 00:50:56,049
<i>a four-year-old child died shortly
after being brought to the emergency room.</i>

863
00:50:56,049 --> 00:50:57,549
<i>You remember that case, right?</i>

864
00:50:57,549 --> 00:50:59,336
<i>According to the medical records at the time,</i>

865
00:50:59,336 --> 00:51:02,344
the abdomen was filled with blood
due to internal organ bleeding,

866
00:51:02,344 --> 00:51:04,194
and there were fractures all over the body,

867
00:51:04,194 --> 00:51:06,640
but the fractures
occurred at different times.

868
00:51:06,640 --> 00:51:09,640
My gosh. What did they do to that child?

869
00:51:09,640 --> 00:51:14,036
A police investigation
revealed horrific child abuse.

870
00:51:14,036 --> 00:51:15,876
The adoptive mom, as the main culprit,
was sentenced to 9 years,

871
00:51:15,876 --> 00:51:19,184
and the biological dad,
Gu Jong Ryeol, got 2 years for neglect.

872
00:51:19,184 --> 00:51:21,020
Their sentences are ridiculous.

873
00:51:21,020 --> 00:51:22,716
The abuse was acknowledged,

874
00:51:22,716 --> 00:51:25,844
but the court found no implied intent
regarding the child's death,

875
00:51:25,844 --> 00:51:29,196
so they were charged with
injury causing death, not murder.

876
00:51:29,196 --> 00:51:33,380
The six-year-old sister also gave
testimony favorable to the parents.

877
00:51:33,380 --> 00:51:35,316
Is there a chance Gu Jong Ryeol
genuinely didn't know?

878
00:51:35,316 --> 00:51:37,749
[Client Information]
The daughter later recanted her testimony.

879
00:51:37,749 --> 00:51:41,140
She said her dad
had abused the child as well.

880
00:51:41,140 --> 00:51:45,649
But it wasn't accepted because her statements
were considered inconsistent.

881
00:51:45,649 --> 00:51:47,852
Where's the daughter now?

882
00:51:47,852 --> 00:51:51,383
She's not living with her dad, is she?

883
00:51:52,244 --> 00:51:55,408
She was taken away right after it happened
and is now in a child care center.

884
00:51:55,408 --> 00:51:58,083
Well, that's a relief.

885
00:51:58,700 --> 00:52:00,716
So what about Gu Jong Ryeol?

886
00:52:01,592 --> 00:52:06,144
I believe he's highly likely to be
Kingfisher's next target.

887
00:52:06,144 --> 00:52:07,388
Who wants to take this one?

888
00:52:07,388 --> 00:52:09,149
- Me.
- I will.

889
00:52:14,110 --> 00:52:15,288
What's going on?

890
00:52:15,288 --> 00:52:19,492
Since when did you become
such in-sync partners?

891
00:52:19,492 --> 00:52:21,388
No way!

892
00:52:21,388 --> 00:52:24,256
Right? There's no way you two are, huh?

893
00:52:24,256 --> 00:52:25,452
No!

894
00:52:25,452 --> 00:52:29,520
Anyway, we need to keep
a low profile for the time being,

895
00:52:29,520 --> 00:52:30,956
so you two handle this case.

896
00:52:30,956 --> 00:52:33,388
And Assistant Manager Ki,
make sure there's solid support.

897
00:52:33,388 --> 00:52:35,652
Understood.

898
00:52:35,652 --> 00:52:37,768
<i>What? Use Gu Jong Ryeol?</i>

899
00:52:37,768 --> 00:52:41,752
We'll set a trap around Gu Jong Ryeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

900
00:52:41,752 --> 00:52:46,668
Are you suggesting we work
with a criminal to set up a sting?

901
00:52:46,668 --> 00:52:48,560
I'm suggesting we use it as an opportunity.

902
00:52:48,560 --> 00:52:51,349
Isn't the evidence too weak
to say for certain that

903
00:52:51,349 --> 00:52:53,324
Gu Jong Ryeol is the next target?

904
00:52:53,324 --> 00:52:56,583
For now, I think it's our only lead
to catching Kingfisher.

905
00:52:56,583 --> 00:52:57,948
Wait.

906
00:52:57,948 --> 00:53:02,296
If we go by what you say,
there's no guarantee he'll use a gun,

907
00:53:02,296 --> 00:53:06,564
so how can we jump into this without knowing
when, where, or how he'll strike?

908
00:53:06,564 --> 00:53:09,908
Deploying equipment and personnel
based on speculation alone

909
00:53:09,908 --> 00:53:12,824
is like banging our heads against a wall.

910
00:53:12,824 --> 00:53:15,488
Mr. Gu, I think this has
a real chance of working.

911
00:53:15,488 --> 00:53:16,792
Please hear me out a little longer...

912
00:53:16,792 --> 00:53:19,432
What more is there to hear?

913
00:53:19,432 --> 00:53:21,132
Mr. Gu!

914
00:53:22,608 --> 00:53:24,308
Go for it.

915
00:53:25,260 --> 00:53:26,960
What?

916
00:53:27,740 --> 00:53:30,288
But you can't make direct
contact with Gu Jong Ryeol.

917
00:53:30,288 --> 00:53:34,260
Teaming up with a criminal to catch
a criminal? Does that make sense?

918
00:53:34,260 --> 00:53:37,336
Second, I can't convince the higher-ups
without solid evidence.

919
00:53:37,336 --> 00:53:40,412
So I can't provide equipment
or personnel support right now.

920
00:53:40,412 --> 00:53:43,976
Third, I can't give you unlimited time.

921
00:53:43,976 --> 00:53:45,640
For now, Mr. Lee, work on
this one on your own.

922
00:53:45,640 --> 00:53:48,240
You two can stake out for 24 hours
or keep surveillance.

923
00:53:48,240 --> 00:53:49,448
You have exactly one week.

924
00:53:49,448 --> 00:53:51,452
If you manage to get any lead
on Kingfisher within that time,

925
00:53:51,452 --> 00:53:53,149
I'll stake my team leader position

926
00:53:53,149 --> 00:53:56,784
and give you all the support you want. Okay?

927
00:53:56,784 --> 00:53:58,484
Alright, meeting's over!

928
00:53:59,683 --> 00:54:00,783
Oh, boy.

929
00:54:00,783 --> 00:54:03,116
- It'll be a waste of effort.
- Oh, dear.

930
00:54:04,341 --> 00:54:06,041
Oh, jeez.

931
00:54:07,083 --> 00:54:09,148
[Used PC Sales and Repair]

932
00:54:09,148 --> 00:54:10,949
Here you go.

933
00:54:14,932 --> 00:54:18,228
The voice recordings
and other data are all still intact, right?

934
00:54:18,228 --> 00:54:22,216
Of course. I only replaced the battery,
so all the data inside is still intact.

935
00:54:33,452 --> 00:54:35,816
Assistant Manager Ki went down first.

936
00:55:03,383 --> 00:55:05,172
You always seem to have venom in your veins.

937
00:55:05,172 --> 00:55:06,560
Of course.

938
00:55:06,560 --> 00:55:08,944
You're very wary.

939
00:55:08,944 --> 00:55:10,572
Did you have a rough childhood?

940
00:55:10,572 --> 00:55:12,352
I had a childhood as miserable as anyone's.

941
00:55:12,352 --> 00:55:14,308
I don't even know what my parents look like.

942
00:55:14,308 --> 00:55:17,160
Must've been nice, not having a dad.

943
00:55:17,160 --> 00:55:19,949
You must at least know when you were born.

944
00:55:19,949 --> 00:55:21,516
I know exactly.

945
00:55:21,516 --> 00:55:24,449
Because I broke a rib on my fifth birthday.

946
00:55:34,196 --> 00:55:37,004
You can break a rib even without a dad.

947
00:55:37,004 --> 00:55:38,716
An arm or a leg too.

948
00:56:02,464 --> 00:56:04,068
I'll back you up too.

949
00:56:04,068 --> 00:56:05,883
Director Yoo!

950
00:56:07,049 --> 00:56:09,783
You're really going to back me up?

951
00:56:13,620 --> 00:56:16,083
Let's see what you two can do.

952
00:56:18,332 --> 00:56:20,356
You're driving too?

953
00:56:20,356 --> 00:56:22,383
Hurry up, let's go.

954
00:56:22,383 --> 00:56:24,083
Come on out!

955
00:56:29,560 --> 00:56:31,716
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

956
00:56:40,904 --> 00:56:42,708
Keep a close watch.

957
00:56:42,708 --> 00:56:44,236
On what?

958
00:56:44,236 --> 00:56:45,852
I mean, Yoo Bo Na.

959
00:56:45,852 --> 00:56:48,316
If something feels off, we'll call off
the meeting immediately.

960
00:56:48,316 --> 00:56:50,016
Ms. Bo Na?

961
00:56:51,576 --> 00:56:54,952
Is something bugging you?

962
00:56:54,952 --> 00:56:58,949
This client makes me think of someone.

963
00:57:00,549 --> 00:57:03,456
Some memories from childhood

964
00:57:03,456 --> 00:57:06,083
don't fade easily, you know.

965
00:57:14,352 --> 00:57:17,080
If he approves it,
he needs to give us their full support.

966
00:57:17,080 --> 00:57:20,316
This isn't really approval,
but it's not a refusal either.

967
00:57:21,220 --> 00:57:24,916
At least assign a few people
to relieve us on the stakeout.

968
00:57:30,272 --> 00:57:33,064
Looks like you have a lot on your mind.

969
00:57:33,064 --> 00:57:38,132
Do you think Kingfisher could be a woman?

970
00:57:38,132 --> 00:57:39,832
Huh?

971
00:57:40,540 --> 00:57:42,640
Well...

972
00:57:42,640 --> 00:57:45,383
I think it's quite possible.

973
00:57:47,892 --> 00:57:49,580
A foreigner?

974
00:57:49,580 --> 00:57:51,916
That seems possible too.

975
00:57:51,916 --> 00:57:53,428
What about a minor?

976
00:57:53,428 --> 00:57:55,283
There's no reason to rule it out.

977
00:57:57,724 --> 00:57:59,424
Right.

978
00:58:00,400 --> 00:58:03,730
Based on my gut,
there's definitely a secret organization

979
00:58:03,730 --> 00:58:05,452
like a "Dark Death Squad" behind Kingfisher.

980
00:58:05,452 --> 00:58:08,204
They disguise themselves as ordinary people,

981
00:58:08,204 --> 00:58:10,900
and when an order comes down, and then, bam!

982
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:13,049
Just watch where you're going.

983
00:58:15,264 --> 00:58:18,448
After 15 years of all-out investigation
and still no arrest,

984
00:58:18,448 --> 00:58:23,583
maybe he's disguised himself
in a way we never imagined.

985
00:59:03,783 --> 00:59:09,000
Being in the field next to you
feels like a dream.

986
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:11,649
I'm not here to make your dream come true.

987
00:59:11,649 --> 00:59:14,683
Next time, wish for something bigger.

988
00:59:15,749 --> 00:59:17,449
Okay.

989
00:59:22,144 --> 00:59:24,649
But why are you really here?

990
00:59:24,649 --> 00:59:27,616
I heard you don't personally
deal with White targets.

991
00:59:29,640 --> 00:59:32,549
Well, it just reminded me of the old days.

992
00:59:37,140 --> 00:59:41,256
Can I ask who your first client was?

993
00:59:41,256 --> 00:59:43,183
My first client...

994
00:59:47,252 --> 00:59:49,749
Well, who should I say it was?

995
00:59:50,620 --> 00:59:52,320
What?

996
00:59:57,216 --> 00:59:59,849
Okay, shall we go?

997
01:00:08,783 --> 01:00:11,216
Client meeting starts.

998
01:00:46,849 --> 01:00:49,656
So he was in the middle of
his working life, huh?

999
01:00:49,656 --> 01:00:52,520
<i>Darn it! Fell again!</i>

1000
01:00:52,520 --> 01:00:55,416
<i>Why do these things keep
crashing all the darn time?</i>

1001
01:00:57,068 --> 01:00:59,716
<i>Grip it tightly.</i>

1002
01:00:59,716 --> 01:01:02,316
<i>Otherwise, you'll break another bone.</i>

1003
01:01:05,083 --> 01:01:06,849
<i>Darn it!</i>

1004
01:01:09,308 --> 01:01:12,283
Oh, this is driving me crazy.

1005
01:01:24,396 --> 01:01:26,716
That punk...

1006
01:01:34,056 --> 01:01:35,700
Ms. Yoo, don't!

1007
01:01:35,700 --> 01:01:37,400
Ms. Oh Hyun Nam!

1008
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:01,616
[Recording]

1009
01:02:01,616 --> 01:02:04,549
[Voice Recording File]

1010
01:02:06,116 --> 01:02:07,983
[Call Recording]

1011
01:02:07,983 --> 01:02:10,216
[June 27, 2018]

1012
01:02:11,749 --> 01:02:15,783
[June 27, 2018]

1013
01:02:33,116 --> 01:02:36,300
You fell because you have no patience,

1014
01:02:36,300 --> 01:02:40,249
yet people blame it all on me.

1015
01:02:41,316 --> 01:02:44,516
They just don't know how to raise tough kids.

1016
01:02:45,383 --> 01:02:47,916
What? Who are you?

1017
01:02:55,224 --> 01:02:57,038
<i>Someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor</i>

1018
01:02:57,038 --> 01:02:59,816
<i>of the emergency stairs at King Tower.</i>

1019
01:03:00,860 --> 01:03:03,568
<i>I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.</i>

1020
01:03:03,568 --> 01:03:08,649
<i>She could have witnessed Kingfisher
or been an accomplice.</i>

1021
01:03:15,812 --> 01:03:19,349
<i>Or she could even be Kingfisher herself.</i>

1022
01:04:43,092 --> 01:04:45,616
So you finally opened the door.

1023
01:04:45,616 --> 01:04:47,272
[Big Precious]
Tae Seong.

1024
01:04:47,272 --> 01:04:49,592
Stay together, or leave her...

1025
01:04:49,592 --> 01:04:52,088
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

1026
01:04:52,088 --> 01:04:54,056
Give me an honest answer.

1027
01:04:54,056 --> 01:04:56,068
So an unavoidable variable
popped up with your husband.

1028
01:04:56,068 --> 01:04:57,616
If I leave for somewhere again...

1029
01:04:57,616 --> 01:04:58,616
Are you going somewhere?

1030
01:04:58,616 --> 01:05:00,349
It looks like our police network was hacked.

1031
01:05:00,349 --> 01:05:03,292
Could there be a Kingfisher operative
inside the police?

1032
01:05:03,292 --> 01:05:06,276
That woman who's your friend's wife...
What does she do for a living?

1033
01:05:06,276 --> 01:05:07,712
We've got a witness.

1034
01:05:07,712 --> 01:05:09,007
[Durumi Electronics]
Could Kingfisher

1035
01:05:09,007 --> 01:05:11,656
be a parent raising a child?

1036
01:05:11,656 --> 01:05:14,849
Is Kingfisher the person
you said you had to protect?
